1 VI. Its handle explanation is dead (healthy at 51,349, crashed at 35,555).\n\n**NEXT**: run 10 = `build_d1_routeb_v7.py`, one edit — save the half-built copy, restart LabVIEW, reopen, take the census in the fresh instance. That is simultaneously the only route to the missing measurement and the test of the cumulative-allocation hypothesis STATUS has carried unconfirmed for two cycles (`docs/cycle27-plan.md` Pre-decided 20).\n\nRetrospective returned **`VIOLATION: none`**. I acted on four of its findings in-cycle rather than carrying them: the misleading \"80 PASS / 0 FAIL\" lead now leads with the crash; the cycle's true ~$9.78 spend is stated to the user; the risk that `guard_peer` stalls run 10 on run 9's `rc=1` log is written into NEXT with its discharge route; and I accepted the L3 finding without argument and relocated the resolved user items — the reviewer was right that \"line-count is the wrong meter\" was a rationale, not a repair.","ttft_ms":2032,"type":"result","duration_ms":4644980,"uuid":"1ecbef51-27b7-48f2-a676-32fc8c8e11bd","ttft_stream_ms":1696,"time_to_request_ms":300,"queued_turn_count":0}
